1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,650
Two audio tracks in. How many come out?

2
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:16,440
No error. One track just vanishes.

3
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:26,590
Track 1: 440 Hz. Track 2: 880 Hz.

4
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:34,210
Two readers: ffprobe, and measured pitch.

5
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:40,900
No -map: 1 audio track, 440 Hz.

6
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:49,500
The 880 Hz track is gone. -c copy: same.

7
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,380
-map 0: both tones present.

8
00:00:55,380 --> 00:01:05,950
-map 0:v -map 0:a:1: only the 880 Hz track.

9
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:12,950
Docs: audio, the stream with the most channels.

10
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:20,830
Track 2 is stereo. Track 1 was still kept.

11
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:31,220
Flag on track 2: output keeps 880 Hz, stereo.

12
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:38,150
Same on ffmpeg 6.1.1 and 8.1.2.

13
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:45,370
Every track: -map 0. One track: name it.

14
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:49,880
Not tested: subtitles, other containers.
